# Custom guides: guide_custom

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`guide_custom()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/guide_custom.html), in the order the
page gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly
cannot draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a list
of what remains.

`guide_custom()` draws any graphical object, a `grid` grob, alongside a plot's legends, with a
title if given one. It belongs to no scale. Giggly has none of it yet: it has no guides, no
legends and no `grid` grobs.

## A grob as a guide

```r
# A standard plot
p <- ggplot(mpg, aes(displ, hwy)) +
  geom_point()

# Define a graphical object
circle <- grid::circleGrob()

# Rendering a grob as a guide
p + guides(custom = guide_custom(circle, title = "My circle"))
```

Not in Giggly yet: `grid` grobs, `guides()` and `guide_custom()`.

## Sizing a grob in relative units

A circle grob made without a radius takes its size from the space it is given, so `width` and
`height` set that space.

```r
# Controlling the size of the grob defined in relative units
p + guides(custom = guide_custom(
  circle, title = "My circle",
  width = unit(2, "cm"), height = unit(2, "cm"))
)
```

Not in Giggly yet: `grid` grobs, `guides()`, and `guide_custom()` with its `width` and `height`
options.

## A grob in absolute units

```r
# Size of grobs in absolute units is taken directly without the need to
# set these manually
p + guides(custom = guide_custom(
  title = "My circle",
  grob = grid::circleGrob(r = unit(1, "cm"))
))
```

Not in Giggly yet: `grid` grobs, `guides()` and `guide_custom()`.
